From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: nt36532e - re-enable touch after system resume

The system PM callbacks only cleared dev_pm_suspend. Unlike the runtime and
panel-follower paths they never re-enabled the interrupt, so after a
successful suspend/resume the controller kept sampling but the driver saw no
frames and touch input stopped until the next full reboot.

Re-arm the IRQ and the awake flag on system resume, matching nvt_ts_resume().
If the panel is not prepared the panel follower owns the state and no IRQ is
armed; the follower callback restores it.

---
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532e/nt36xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532e/nt36xxx.c
@@ -2600,6 +2600,14 @@
 	NVT_LOG("system resume from pm_suspend");
 	ts->dev_pm_suspend = false;
 	complete(&ts->dev_pm_suspend_completion);
+	/* The runtime path re-enables the IRQ; system resume must too, or the
+	 * controller keeps sampling while the driver sees no frames. When a
+	 * panel follower is present and the panel is down, the follower's
+	 * prepared callback restores scanning instead. */
+	if (!ts->panel_follower_registered || ts->panel_on) {
+		nvt_irq_enable(true);
+		bTouchIsAwake = 1;
+	}
 	NVT_LOG("system resume from pm_suspend2");
 	return 0;
 }
